James wanted to create a short story for his 5-year-old son, who enjoys scary themes like monsters and vampires. He sought an early reader format that features a bad-guy protagonist and involves trickery, while allowing his son to practice reading simple words. I provided a 4-page story titled “Nip the Bat,” featuring a small bat named Nip who attempts to scare a dog but faces unexpected trouble with a group of bats. James then requested a version with more "Epic/Iliad energy." I responded with “Nip and the Night Raid,” emphasizing boasting, pride, and a daring night raid against a hound, while keeping it accessible for early readers. This version maintained elements of humor, adventure, and a confident lead, concluding with Nip’s defiant promise to raid again. James was satisfied with both stories and considered additional variations for his son.
